1
00:00:00,097 --> 00:00:01,833
A million people's salaries.

2
00:00:02,264 --> 00:00:05,847
Ninety-nine megabytes — twenty-six million tokens.

3
00:00:06,278 --> 00:00:08,194
No AI can read a file this size.

4
00:00:08,653 --> 00:00:11,069
And you would never paste it into one anyway.

5
00:00:11,579 --> 00:00:13,657
So watch one analyse it anyway,

6
00:00:14,133 --> 00:00:16,443
without ever seeing a single row.

7
00:00:16,933 --> 00:00:19,765
Every column is graded before the agent is told

8
00:00:19,765 --> 00:00:20,951
the file exists.

9
00:00:21,347 --> 00:00:23,974
Name, email, employee ID — sealed.

10
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:25,530
It cannot group by them,

11
00:00:25,938 --> 00:00:28,158
filter on them, or ever receive them.

12
00:00:28,656 --> 00:00:31,794
Eight WebMCP tools, and notice what is missing:

13
00:00:32,266 --> 00:00:33,886
there is no run_sql.

14
00:00:34,294 --> 00:00:36,590
The agent cannot write a query at all.

15
00:00:37,011 --> 00:00:38,044
It fills in a form,

16
00:00:38,337 --> 00:00:39,549
and the page compiles it.

17
00:00:39,983 --> 00:00:43,018
The same eight tools appear in ChatGPT and in

18
00:00:43,018 --> 00:00:44,205
Chrome behind the flag.

19
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:46,462
This is the standard, not one app.

20
00:00:46,968 --> 00:00:47,476
Schema.

21
00:00:47,893 --> 00:00:48,895
Cohort comparison.

22
00:00:49,325 --> 00:00:49,716
Chart.

23
00:00:50,132 --> 00:00:53,309
Each one across all one million rows in under

24
00:00:53,322 --> 00:00:54,260
a tenth of a second.

25
00:00:54,676 --> 00:00:56,265
And look at what just happened with that chart:

26
00:00:56,656 --> 00:00:57,828
the agent asked for it,

27
00:00:58,062 --> 00:01:00,197
I can see it, and the agent got back

28
00:01:00,210 --> 00:01:01,200
one word — drawn.

29
00:01:01,669 --> 00:01:03,674
Three percent pay gap at the junior levels,

30
00:01:03,921 --> 00:01:05,783
thirteen at the senior ones.

31
00:01:06,297 --> 00:01:07,599
Ask who is paid most,

32
00:01:07,990 --> 00:01:09,032
and it refuses.

33
00:01:09,448 --> 00:01:12,026
A maximum is one real person's salary.

34
00:01:12,456 --> 00:01:14,865
And the refusal tells the agent what to ask

35
00:01:14,865 --> 00:01:17,339
instead, so it recovers on the next turn.

36
00:01:17,854 --> 00:01:20,873
But a counter reading zero is just this page

37
00:01:20,886 --> 00:01:22,535
marking its own homework.

38
00:01:22,961 --> 00:01:25,647
So the page revokes its own network access.

39
00:01:26,072 --> 00:01:28,719
Watch me try to leak the data on purpose.

40
00:01:29,237 --> 00:01:29,623
Fetch.

41
00:01:30,035 --> 00:01:30,740
XHR.

42
00:01:30,979 --> 00:01:31,830
WebSocket.

43
00:01:32,283 --> 00:01:32,615
Beacon.

44
00:01:33,041 --> 00:01:34,025
Tracking pixel.

45
00:01:34,437 --> 00:01:36,099
Chrome refuses all five.

46
00:01:36,619 --> 00:01:39,527
And this is every byte the agent actually received.

47
00:01:39,961 --> 00:01:41,974
Not a summary — the literal text.

48
00:01:42,396 --> 00:01:43,343
Search it for a name,

49
00:01:43,738 --> 00:01:44,554
and there is none.

50
00:01:45,070 --> 00:01:46,622
Ninety-nine megabytes in.

51
00:01:47,075 --> 00:01:47,900
Kilobytes out.

52
00:01:48,353 --> 00:01:49,287
Zero rows.

53
00:01:49,726 --> 00:01:52,213
And it holds: ten million rows,

54
00:01:52,433 --> 00:01:56,375
a full gigabyte, every query still under a second.

55
00:01:56,842 --> 00:02:00,413
Blindfold — analyse a file your AI could never read.
